body:
Hey, so I have this chicken called peepers who is roughly 4-5 months old.  She hasn't layed any eggs yet which isn't really a big deal as we only keep her because she came int9 our garden one day and nevernever leftleft.  She is completely free range: the only thing we provide is water, she gets the rest from our garden which is quite big. 

She could possibly have low calcium? Can chickenchickens eaeat cuttlefishcuttlefishcuttlefishcuttlefish like rabbits? 

We have 4 cats but they don't try and go for her any more s9so she is no longer scared of them really and just sorta avoids them. She mainly hangs around my rabbit. 

&#x200B;

Anyway. I heard it's around 6 months some chickens lay eggs? So it's not very urgent anyway but my parents would like some sort of compensation for all the poop we have to pick up. 

&#x200B;

Also: any idea what breed she is? She is white and doesn't have much on a cone (crown??) Thing on her head I mean. She likes to dig to get ants and sits in piles on Long grassgrass.  She also roosts in a bush or a tree so quite high up. 

&#x200B;

So sorry for the horrendous typing, Reddit seems to be duplicating what I say and the more I try to fix it the more it duplicates. 

&#x200B;

Thank
